{"id":"CVE-2011-1468","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2011-03-20T01:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T22:28:41.435Z","description":"Multiple memory leaks in the OpenSSL extension in PHP before 5.3.6 might allow remote attackers to cause a denial of service (memory consumption) via (1) plaintext data to the openssl_encrypt function or (2) ciphertext data to the openssl_decrypt function.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2011:053","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2011:053"},{"url":"http://www.php.net/ChangeLog-5.php","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/Security-announce/2011//Oct/msg00003.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2011-10-12-3"},{"url":"http://bugs.php.net/bug.php?id=54060","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.redhat.com/support/errata/RHSA-2011-1423.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2011:1423"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/46977","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"46977"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2011/0744","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2011-0744"},{"url":"http://support.apple.com/kb/HT5002","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://bugs.php.net/bug.php?id=54061","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"35487","title":"PHP < 5.3.6 'OpenSSL' Extension - 'openssl_decrypt' Ciphertext Data Memory Leak Denial of Service","type":"dos","platform":"php","date":"2011-03-08","verified":"1"},{"edb":"35486","title":"PHP < 5.3.6 'OpenSSL' Extension - 'openssl_encrypt' Plaintext Data Memory Leak Denial of Service","type":"dos","platform":"php","date":"2011-03-08","verified":"1"}],"vendors":["openssl","php"]}
{"id":"CVE-2011-1473","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2012-06-16T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T22:28:41.480Z","description":"OpenSSL before 0.9.8l, and 0.9.8m through 1.x, does not properly restrict client-initiated renegotiation within the SSL and TLS protocols, which might make it easier for remote attackers to cause a denial of service (CPU consumption) by performing many renegotiations within a single connection, a different vulnerability than CVE-2011-5094.  NOTE: it can also be argued that it is the responsibility of server deployments, not a security library, to prevent or limit renegotiation when it is inappropriate within a specific environment","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://vincent.bernat.im/en/blog/2011-ssl-dos-mitigation.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.ietf.org/mail-archive/web/tls/current/msg07567.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[tls] 20110315 Re: SSL Renegotiation DOS"},{"url":"http://www.ietf.org/mail-archive/web/tls/current/msg07577.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[tls] 20110318 Re: SSL Renegotiation DOS"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=707065","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://archives.neohapsis.com/archives/bugtraq/2014-02/0061.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20140214 ESA-2014-009: RSA BSAFE SSL-J Multiple Vulnerabilities"},{"url":"http://www.educatedguesswork.org/2011/10/ssltls_and_computational_dos.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2011/07/08/2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20110708 SSL renegotiation DoS CVE-2011-1473"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=133951357207000&w=2","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"SSRT100852"},{"url":"http://www.ietf.org/mail-archive/web/tls/current/msg07576.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[tls] 20110318 Re: SSL Renegotiation DOS"},{"url":"http://orchilles.com/2011/03/ssl-renegotiation-dos.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.ietf.org/mail-archive/web/tls/current/msg07553.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[tls] 20110315 SSL Renegotiation DOS"},{"url":"http://www.ietf.org/mail-archive/web/tls/current/msg07564.html","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[tls] 20110315 Re: SSL Renegotiation DOS"},{"url":"https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/142b93d261e8ac7c5ceffdce848d622404abc1c286bbc999f43a9e10%40%3Cdev.rocketmq.apache.org%3E","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[rocketmq-dev] 20190527 [GitHub] [rocketmq] bix29 opened a new issue #1233: TLS Client-initiated renegotiation attack (CVE-2011-1473)"},{"url":"https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/6121becfdd23f9aeb675d5db80616536277d5931d6cde9dca292e509%40%3Cdev.rocketmq.apache.org%3E","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[rocketmq-dev] 20190801 [GitHub] [rocketmq] duhenglucky commented on issue #1233: TLS Client-initiated renegotiation attack (CVE-2011-1473)"},{"url":"https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/8be38d35654441140db8eb3f7433524b3653ac3fdc26e2fa94626a3a%40%3Cdev.rocketmq.apache.org%3E","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[rocketmq-dev] 20191024 [GitHub] [rocketmq] Journey-x commented on issue #1233: TLS Client-initiated renegotiation attack (CVE-2011-1473)"},{"url":"https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/r1e33410bb5c81536e7fe14b51fa83e7bfd9445db61fd10c134792bde%40%3Cdev.rocketmq.apache.org%3E","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[rocketmq-dev] 20200305 [GitHub] [rocketmq] ShadowySpirits commented on issue #1233: TLS Client-initiated renegotiation attack (CVE-2011-1473)"},{"url":"https://lists.apache.org/thread.html/r298a09a2b98446b27217d719e877c643b6d13fac0bcafe04696a446b%40%3Cdev.rocketmq.apache.org%3E","tags":["mailing-list",