{"id":"CVE-2011-1945","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2011-05-31T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T22:46:00.682Z","description":"The elliptic curve cryptography (ECC) subsystem in OpenSSL 1.0.0d and earlier, when the Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm (ECDSA) is used for the ECDHE_ECDSA cipher suite, does not properly implement curves over binary fields, which makes it easier for context-dependent attackers to determine private keys via a timing attack and a lattice calculation.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2011:136","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2011:136"},{"url":"http://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/id/MAPG-8FENZ3","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2011:137","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2011:137"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2011/dsa-2309","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-2309"},{"url":"http://support.apple.com/kb/HT5784","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/security-announce/2013/Jun/msg00000.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2013-06-04-1"},{"url":"https://hermes.opensuse.org/messages/8760466","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2011:0634"},{"url":"http://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/id/536044","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_CERT-VN"],"name":"VU#536044"},{"url":"https://hermes.opensuse.org/messages/8764170","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"SUSE-SU-2011:0636"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/44935","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"44935"},{"url":"http://eprint.iacr.org/2011/232.pdf","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2011-3207","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2011-09-22T10:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T23:29:56.260Z","description":"crypto/x509/x509_vfy.c in OpenSSL 1.0.x before 1.0.0e does not initialize certain structure members, which makes it easier for remote attackers to bypass CRL validation by using a nextUpdate value corresponding to a time in the past.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=133226187115472&w=2","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_HP"],"name":"HPSBMU02752"},{"url":"http://www-01.ibm.com/support/docview.wss?uid=ssg1S1004564","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/package-announce/2012-November/092905.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2012-18035"},{"url":"http://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/package-announce/2011-September/065744.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2011-12233"},{"url":"http://cvs.openssl.org/chngview?cn=21349","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/45956","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"45956"},{"url":"http://www.mandriva.com/security/advisories?name=MDVSA-2011:137","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_MANDRIVA"],"name":"MDVSA-2011:137"},{"url":"http://lists.fedoraproject.org/pipermail/package-announce/2011-September/065712.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2011-12281"},{"url":"http://support.apple.com/kb/HT5784","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://lists.apple.com/archives/security-announce/2013/Jun/msg00000.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_APPLE"],"name":"APPLE-SA-2013-06-04-1"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=736087","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id?1026012","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTR