{"id":"CVE-2011-4121","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2019-11-26T04:35:56.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T00:01:50.387Z","description":"The OpenSSL extension of Ruby (Git trunk) versions after 2011-09-01 up to 2011-11-03 always generated an exponent value of '1' to be used for private RSA key generation. A remote attacker could use this flaw to bypass or corrupt integrity of services, depending on strong private RSA keys generation mechanism.","cwe":["Other"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL","product":"OpenSSL extension of Ruby (Git trunk)","versions":["affected versions after 2011-09-01 up to 2011-11-03"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2011-4121","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2011-4121","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/cve-2011-4121","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2013/07/01/1","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2011-4354","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2012-01-27T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T00:01:51.637Z","description":"crypto/bn/bn_nist.c in OpenSSL before 0.9.8h on 32-bit platforms, as used in stunnel and other products, in certain circumstances involving ECDH or ECDHE cipher suites, uses an incorrect modular reduction algorithm in its implementation of the P-256 and P-384 NIST elliptic curves, which allows remote attackers to obtain the private key of a TLS server via multiple handshake attempts.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://crypto.di.uminho.pt/CACE/CT-RSA2012-openssl-src.zip","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=757909","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://openwall.com/lists/oss-security/2011/12/01/6","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_MLIST"],"name":"[oss-security] 20111201 CVE-2011-4354 OpenSSL 0.9.8g (32-bit builds) bug leaks ECC private keys"},{"url":"http://eprint.iacr.org/2011/633","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://rt.openssl.org/Ticket/Display.html?id=1593&user=guest&pass=guest","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://cvs.openssl.org/filediff?f=openssl/crypto/bn/bn_nist.c&v1=1.14&v2=1.21","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2012/dsa-2390","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-2390"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?t=119271238800004","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
